      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original. No other-angle proposal or semantic judgment was read. Letter to a Friend is banked as the established title with unique Friend/Letter members; the bracketed author remains explanatory even though the glossary contains the expanded quotation. The plural rnams is fused into spirits, not semantically absent. Each bound ang contributes even, but it cannot be detached as a standalone syllable or placed under a moon/sun parent whose English excludes even; both contributions are omitted with this reason, not falsely nulled. Light, they, the reprise sensation, and the expanded It is a fact frame stay unwrapped. Capital In is verse lineation. C15:417 and C18:1131 match all three text fields; P7:26 matches English with Tibetan orthographic/punctuation differences, without establishing publication independence. No source or hgm_gloss is changed."
